ytest -m' in run and '--dist' in run`, which would MISS `python -m pytest` (no `pytest -m` token) and the bare structured-output `pytest tests/...` (no `-m`).","Several comment/prose lines mention 'pytest' and must be excluded to avoid false positives: `_build-and-test.yml:684` (a `# --timeout ...` comment), `test.yml:7` and `test.yml:10` (header comments), and comments inside structured-output-baseline.yml."],"finding":"The new exhaustive parity sweep's detection rule for 'pytest in command position' is under-specified against the heterogeneous invocation forms actually present, and a naive substring match risks both misses and false positives.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa370f65286a33cac","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Anti-regression section; AC8","norm_id":"n3ea3eb4c78410aa7","priority":0.603,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["A future lane invokes pytest as `python -m pytest` and the sweep's matcher only looks for the `pytest -m` token, so the new lane ships unguarded despite the 'no allowlist, exhaustive' promise.","The matcher keys on the substring 'pytest' per line and trips on a comment mentioning pytest, forcing a bogus timeout assertion on a non-invoking step."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that the sweep strips shell comments and matches a pytest command token (`pytest` or `python -m pytest`, optionally path-prefixed) at command position on each non-comment run line, independent of `-m`/`--dist`; AC8's temporary-flag-removal check should be run against a lane in EACH invocation form (e.g. both the bare-`pytest` structured-output step and a `python -m pytest` step) to prove the detector sees them.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the parity matcher precisely (which invocation forms count as 'pytest in command position', e.g. `pytest`, `python -m pytest`, `poetry run pytest`) and add a fixture/assertion in AC8 that proves the sweep detects each form, not just a single flag removal on one form.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["E2","E6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'collecting every step whose `run` body invokes pytest in command position'","'deliberately an exhaustive sweep with no allowlist'","AC8 verifies by removing ONE flag — proving detection of one form, not that all invocation forms are recognized"],"finding":"AC8's parity sweep relies on detecting 'every step whose run body invokes pytest in command position', but the plan never specifies the matcher, so invocation forms like `python -m pytest`, `poetry run pytest`, or pytest inside a shell pipeline could be silently missed — a false-pass in the exact anti-regression mechanism meant to close the class.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fecda36bcda150c5a","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Anti-regression section / AC8","norm_id":"n33b9f305599d9fd3","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["